{
 "tickets": [
  {
   "id": "gen-201",
   "subject": "Missing lab results coming through our interface",
   "body": "Hello, I am a bit perplexed by what is happening with our diagnostic feeds today. Usually, the blood work and pathology reports from our main regional lab drop straight into our incoming queue by morning, but nothing has appeared since Tuesday. I checked the integration settings tab and the green connection indicator is lit up, so I am not sure why the actual data packets are not populating. We have several patients waiting for their follow-up reviews, so any light you can shed on why the conduit seems quiet would be greatly appreciated."
  },
  {
   "id": "gen-202",
   "subject": "Inquiry Regarding Online Patient Booking Restrictions",
   "body": "Good morning. We are currently reviewing our web portal configuration and wish to restrict online patient scheduling so that only routine physicals can be booked through the public link. Could you please advise on the proper steps to limit these visit types and exclude certain providers from the web-booking roster? Thank you for your assistance with this matter."
  },
  {
   "id": "gen-203",
   "subject": "Diagnostic Interface Feed Disruption",
   "body": "Hello Support Team, we have noticed that diagnostic results from our primary reference laboratory have stopped populating in our incoming queues as of this morning. The system interface dashboard shows an active connection, but no new pathology files are being received. Please investigate this feed interruption at your earliest convenience."
  },
  {
   "id": "gen-204",
   "subject": "Online booking restrictions",
   "body": "How do I restrict online patient bookings to specific providers and visit types? I need to stop patients from scheduling procedures through the portal. Please provide instructions."
  },
  {
   "id": "gen-205",
   "subject": "Where did our lab results go?",
   "body": "Hi there, I am reaching out because I am really confused about our lab feeds. Yesterday everything was coming in fine, but today when I opened up the diagnostic review section, it was completely empty. I know for a fact our reference lab sent over at least a dozen reports this morning because the courier dropped off hard copies, but nothing is showing up in our software inbox. I tried restarting my workstation and checking the connection status page under admin settings, and it says everything is running normally. Could someone please check on our backend data stream to see why these reports are getting stuck?"
  },
  {
   "id": "gen-206",
   "subject": "Password Policy Update and Staff Reset Assistance",
   "body": "Hello, I am writing to request instructions on how to enforce stricter password complexity requirements for all staff accounts across our practice. Additionally, one of our billing associates needs their password reset following an accidental lockout. Thank you for your guidance on implementing these security measures."
  },
  {
   "id": "gen-207",
   "subject": "Urgent Concern Regarding Lab Result Routing and Privacy",
   "body": "Dear Support Team, we are writing to report a serious workflow issue regarding how incoming diagnostic results are signed off and routed. Earlier today, abnormal lab findings for a patient were inadvertently routed to a covering physician's queue while also appearing on an incorrect viewable list accessible by administrative staff members who should not be seeing such clinical details. We are deeply concerned about this breach of information and need immediate clarification on how to properly isolate abnormal result notifications and restrict sign-off permissions exclusively to licensed medical providers. Please contact us urgently to review our routing configuration and ensure patient data privacy is maintained."
  },
  {
   "id": "gen-208",
   "subject": "Frustrated with pharmacy substitution alerts and out of stock messaging",
   "body": "I am completely fed up with how the system handles out-of-stock medication notifications. Every time I try to switch a patient's prescription to an alternative therapeutic agent because the local pharmacy is out, the software loops me back to the original drug profile instead of saving the substitution. I spent twenty minutes this afternoon clicking through pharmacy messaging prompts for a patient, only for the interface to clear my notes and force me to start the electronic prescribing sequence all over again. This is wasting a massive amount of clinical time during our busy afternoon hours, and I need to know why the substitution workflow is malfunctioning so badly right now."
  },
  {
   "id": "gen-209",
   "subject": "Trouble setting up a series of recurring appointments for a patient",
   "body": "Hello, I am having a really confusing time trying to book a series of weekly visits for a patient who needs regular check-ins over the next three months. Every time I select the recurring appointment option and pick Tuesdays at 10 AM, the system lets me choose the pattern, but then it throws up an error message saying there is a scheduling conflict on a date three weeks out. When I go to look at that specific Tuesday, the provider's calendar looks completely open, so I cannot figure out what block or rule is triggering the conflict. I tried canceling the whole sequence and starting over twice, but I keep running into the exact same wall and I am not sure which schedule setting is causing the block."
  },
  {
   "id": "gen-210",
   "subject": "Practice details and NPI updates not saving",
   "body": "Our entire practice is currently unable to update our provider identifiers and location addresses because the update settings page keeps crashing when we click save. Is the system down right now?"
  }
 ]
}
